From 3a168af5850113f7bf2f1507e34688ecc44b756c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:11:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] 0987 redfin: swap-complete ticks and a swap trace
 (sweetswapdone, p swapdone)

backboardd only turns on IOMFB notification type 5 (every klog: "notifications
type 5 on/off", never another type) and learns that a swap is done from
SwapWait (sel 6 [id, 0x80000000, 0], for the swap before and then the one just
ended); upstream HakiOS also sends only type 5. So a swap-complete event can
only reach CA as a type-5 tick. sweetswapdone/p swapdone MASK: 1 = a tick once
a frame's present is done (blit fence landed, CPU copy done, direct scanout
latched), at least sweetpace_min after the last one; 2 = trace the next 256
events (SwapBegin/End/Wait in/out, backboardd's GPU submits, ticks, swap done)
with thread ids, printed as SWEET SWAPTRACE once full (p swapdone trace re-arms).
Default 0: nothing changes.
---
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAccelerator.cpp |   4 +
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp | 125 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 129 insertions(+)

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAccelerator.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAccelerator.cpp
